1. DEFINITIONS

1.1. "License" means this SLI Hosting Restricted License, Version 1.0.

1.2. "Licensor" means each individual or legal entity that owns or controls copyright or other applicable intellectual property rights in the Software and makes those rights available under this License.

1.3. "You" and "Your" mean the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this License.

1.4. "Your Organization" means You and, where applicable, any legal entity, sole proprietorship, partnership, or other organization that directly or indirectly controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with You.

"Control" means the power to direct an entity's management or policies through ownership, voting rights, contractual arrangements, or otherwise.

1.5. "Software" means the copyrighted software, source code, executable code, documentation, and other materials expressly made available under this License.

1.6. "Covered Work" means the Software, any Modified Version, any Derivative Work, and any Combined Work to the extent subject to this License.

1.7. "Modified Version" means a version of the Software containing additions, deletions, adaptations, corrections, replacements, or other changes to its copyright-protected material.

1.8. "Derivative Work" means a work based upon or derived from the Software that requires authorization from a Licensor under applicable copyright law.

1.9. "Combined Work" means a work incorporating the Software with other components where the resulting combination constitutes a derivative work or otherwise requires authorization from a Licensor under applicable copyright law.

1.10. "Corresponding Source" means the complete source code of a Covered Work in the preferred form for making modifications, together with all materials reasonably necessary to build, install, execute, maintain, and modify that Covered Work.

Corresponding Source includes, where applicable:

(a) Source code for all covered components;

(b) Build scripts and build configuration;

(c) Installation and deployment instructions;

(d) Interface definitions;

(e) Dependency manifests and applicable lockfiles;

(f) Database schemas and migration scripts;

(g) Configuration templates;

(h) Scripts required to generate executable forms;

(i) Modifications to covered dependencies; and

(j) Other materials necessary to reproduce the functionality of the Covered Work from its source.

Corresponding Source does not include credentials, private cryptographic keys, personal information, confidential production data, or independently licensed system components that are not part of the Covered Work.

1.11. "Convey" means to distribute, publish, transfer, or otherwise provide copies of a Covered Work to another individual or legal entity.

1.12. "Operate" means to execute, deploy, maintain, or make a Covered Work available for ongoing functional use, including personal, organizational, production, staging, or network-accessible use.

1.13. "Operational Use" means use of a Covered Work outside Development Testing, including ongoing personal use, organizational use, production deployment, or provision of functionality to users.

1.14. "Development Testing" means temporary execution reasonably necessary to develop, debug, evaluate, or test modifications before Operational Use.

Development Testing does not include continuous production use, ongoing organizational use, or making a Covered Work available as a functional service to ordinary users.

1.15. "Operational Modification" means any modification to copyright-protected material forming part of a Covered Work that is used outside Development Testing.

Changes solely to deployment-specific values, including hostnames, ports, credentials, environment variables, or resource allocations, do not independently constitute an Operational Modification unless they alter copyright-protected source code or form part of a modified Covered Work.

1.16. "Network Interaction" means interaction with a running Covered Work through a computer network, including through websites, application programming interfaces, remote clients, or other network interfaces.

1.17. "Internal Use" means operation of a Covered Work by an individual or organization for its own activities, including commercial business operations, without providing the Covered Work as an independent software service to another organization.

1.18. "Authorized Participants" means employees, contractors, contributors, customers, suppliers, or other individuals interacting with a Covered Work in connection with the operator's own activities.

1.19. "Third-Party Hosting" means operating, providing, or making available a Covered Work, directly or indirectly, so that another individual or organization may obtain the functionality of the Covered Work as a software service for its own independent purposes.

Third-Party Hosting includes managed applications, hosted software products, white-label services, Software-as-a-Service offerings, and substantially equivalent arrangements.

1.20. "Public Source Location" means an internet-accessible location from which any person may obtain the complete Corresponding Source without payment, mandatory account creation, identity verification, or discretionary approval.

Ordinary technical measures necessary to protect infrastructure against abuse are permitted, provided they do not materially obstruct legitimate access.

1.21. "Required Notice" means a plain-text notice supplied by a Licensor and expressly identified by the prefix "Required Notice:".

1.22. "Cure" means cessation of violating conduct, restoration of compliance with all applicable provisions of this License, and completion of reasonable and practicable corrective measures addressing the consequences of the violation.

Cure does not require reversal of consequences that cannot reasonably be reversed, but does require all reasonably practicable steps to remedy continuing effects. Cure does not extinguish liability for the original violation.

1.23. "Notice" means a written communication identifying an alleged violation of this License, the affected Software or Covered Work, the applicable Licensor, and the conduct alleged to constitute the violation.

1.24. "Notice Date" means the calendar date on which a Notice is successfully dispatched in accordance with Section 12.

