6.5. In determining whether an integrated component forms part of a Combined Work, relevant circumstances may include:

(a) Incorporation of copyright-protected code;

(b) Shared internal implementation;

(c) Modification of covered interfaces or components;

(d) Technical interdependence;

(e) Distribution as an integrated program; and

(f) Whether the integration constitutes a derivative work under applicable law.

6.6. Mere communication through an API, network protocol, or inter-process interface does not automatically establish that independently developed software is a Combined Work.

6.7. Mere aggregation of independent programs does not automatically subject those programs to this License.

