8. HOSTING RESTRICTIONS

8.1. Except as expressly authorized in writing by every applicable rights holder whose permission is required, Third-Party Hosting is prohibited.

8.2. This prohibition applies regardless of whether:

(a) The service is free or paid;

(b) The service generates revenue;

(c) Access is restricted to selected customers;

(d) The service is operated by a nonprofit organization;

(e) The Software is modified or rebranded;

(f) Users interact with the Covered Work directly;

(g) Users interact through an intermediary application;

(h) The Covered Work operates as a backend service;

(i) Hosting is provided for one customer or multiple customers;

(j) The service is described as managed infrastructure, consulting, support, or another arrangement; or

(k) The service is operated through a third-party infrastructure provider.

8.3. Internal Use is permitted, including Internal Use for commercial business operations.

8.4. Access by Authorized Participants does not independently constitute Third-Party Hosting where the Covered Work is operated for the organization's own activities.

8.5. A deployment constitutes Third-Party Hosting where an external organization receives the Covered Work's functionality for its independent operations as a service provided by the operator.

8.6. Third-Party Hosting includes white-label services, managed deployments, hosted applications, and services in which the Covered Work provides substantial functionality through another application.

8.7. The absence of a direct payment or contractual relationship between the operator and end users does not exempt an otherwise prohibited hosted service.

8.8. An organization may use third-party infrastructure providers to host a Covered Work for its own Internal Use, provided the infrastructure provider does not independently offer the Covered Work's functionality as a service to other customers.

8.9. Activities undertaken through affiliates, subsidiaries, parent entities, contractors, intermediaries, or other persons acting on Your behalf shall be considered when determining compliance with this License.

8.10. You may not use organizational, contractual, or technical arrangements to circumvent restrictions that would otherwise apply to Your activities.

8.11. Legitimate Internal Use within Your Organization is permitted, provided the Covered Work is not offered as an independent hosted software service to unaffiliated third parties.

8.12. A Licensor may authorize otherwise prohibited hosting through a separate written agreement.

8.13. Authorization from one rights holder does not override rights held by another.

